Subject: [PATCH] Song Where: reject generic sign-up pages, reframe UX, curate
 sources
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three targeted fixes for the bait-and-switch problem where "View
opportunity" links led to generic platform sign-up pages:

1. URL specificity filter — isSpecificSubmissionUrl() rejects domain
   roots and generic single-segment paths (/submit, /apply, /briefs,
   /musiccreators, etc.) at the quality gate. Only URLs with IDs,
   deep paths, or platform-specific slugs pass through.

2. UX reframing — "View opportunity →" becomes "View on {Platform} →"
   with explicit context about where the link goes, submission cost,
   and a note to verify requirements at the source.

3. Watchlist curation — removed Groover (playlist pitching, not sync)
   and So Alive Music Conference (single annual event, not a brief
   source). Annotated remaining 10 sources.

